.Dd August 8, 2026
.Dt XTC_SCOPE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xtc_scope ,
.Nm xtc_scope_open ,
.Nm xtc_scope_defer ,
.Nm xtc_scope_close ,
.Nm xtc_bracket ,
.Nm xtc_uncancelable ,
.Nm xtc_cancel_poll ,
.Nm xtc_cancel_requested
.Nd runtime-enforced resource scope and cancellation masking
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In xtc.h
.In xtc_proc.h
.Ft xtc_scope_t *
.Fn xtc_scope_open "void"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_scope_defer "xtc_scope_t *s" "xtc_finalizer_fn fn" "void *arg"
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_scope_close "xtc_scope_t *s"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_bracket "int (*acquire)(void **res, void *ud)" "int (*use)(void *res, void *ud)" "void (*release)(void *res, void *ud)" "void *ud"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_uncancelable "int (*body)(void *ud)" "void *ud"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_cancel_poll "int (*body)(void *ud)" "void *ud"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_cancel_requested "void"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These calls make resource release and cancellation
.Em mechanisms
rather than conventions: a finalizer registered in an open scope runs
on
.Em every
exit path of the enclosing process, and cancellation is composable
through masking.  They are the C analogue of Cats Effect's
.Vt Resource ,
.Fn bracket ,
and
.Fn MonadCancel.uncancelable .
.Ss Resource scope
A scope is a dynamically-scoped region on the calling process.
.Fn xtc_scope_open
opens one and returns a handle (or
.Dv NULL
off a process or on resource exhaustion).
.Fn xtc_scope_defer
registers a finalizer
.Fa fn Ns Pq Fa arg
into the scope.
.Fn xtc_scope_close
runs the deferred finalizers in strict LIFO order and releases the
scope.
.Pp
The guarantee is that the finalizers run
.Em on every exit path
while the scope is open, not only on
.Fn xtc_scope_close :
a normal return, an
.Xr xtc_exit_self 3 ,
an asynchronous kill
.Pq Xr xtc_exit_pid 3 ,
and a fault-guard-contained crash all run them.  A scope is pushed as
a marker on the same per-process recovery registry that releases file
descriptors, locks, and memory contexts on an unwind
.Pq see Xr xtc_proc 3 ,
so the finalizers ride the same LIFO cleanup.  Scopes nest: an outer
unwind closes the inner scopes first.
.Ss Bracket
.Fn xtc_bracket
is the load-bearing acquire/use/release sugar.
.Fa acquire
runs abort-masked
.Pq see Fn xtc_uncancelable
so that
.Fa release
is always registered before cancellation can be observed; it writes
the resource through
.Fa res
and returns
.Dv XTC_OK
on success (any other code aborts the bracket and nothing else runs).
.Fa use
then runs and its return value is returned by
.Fn xtc_bracket .
.Fa release
runs on
.Em every
exit path of
.Fa use
\(em normal return, error, kill, or contained crash.
.Fa ud
threads a caller context through all three callbacks.
.Ss Cancellation masking
Cancellation in xtc is cooperative: a running fiber observes an
asynchronous kill only at a park point
.Pq a yield, receive, or sleep .
.Fn xtc_uncancelable
runs
.Fa body Ns Pq Fa ud
with cancellation
.Em masked :
a kill delivered at a park point inside the region is deferred, not
acted on, and is observed only when the region returns.  This is what
lets a resource acquired in the region always register its release
before cancellation unwinds the fiber \(em without it, guaranteed
release has a finalizer-eating race.  Masking nests
.Pq a per-process counter .
.Pp
.Fn xtc_cancel_poll
is the escape hatch
.Pq Cats Effect's Fn poll :
inside a masked body it runs
.Fa body
with the mask temporarily lifted so cancellation
.Em is
observed for that sub-region; a kill already deferred by the enclosing
mask fires at the poll site before
.Fa body
runs.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_cancel_requested
returns non-zero if cancellation is pending for the calling process
\(em either requested and not yet delivered, or deferred by a mask \(em
so a masked region can choose to unwind early and cleanly.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn xtc_scope_open
returns a scope handle, or
.Dv NULL
off a process or when the recovery registry is full.
.Fn xtc_scope_defer
returns
.Dv XTC_OK ,
.Dv XTC_E_INVAL
on a bad argument or a closed scope, or
.Dv XTC_E_RESOURCE
past the per-scope finalizer limit.
.Fn xtc_bracket ,
.Fn xtc_uncancelable ,
and
.Fn xtc_cancel_poll
return the value returned by
.Fa use
or
.Fa body ,
or
.Dv XTC_E_INVAL
if a required callback is
.Dv NULL .
.Fn xtc_cancel_requested
returns 1 if cancellation is pending, else 0
.Pq including off a process .
.Sh EXAMPLES
Acquire a buffer, use it, and release it on every exit path:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static int acq(void **res, void *ud) {
	(void)ud;
	*res = xtc_malloc(4096);
	return *res ? XTC_OK : XTC_E_RESOURCE;
}
static int use(void *res, void *ud) {
	(void)ud;
	return do_work(res);   /* released even if this kills/faults */
}
static void rel(void *res, void *ud) { (void)ud; xtc_free(res); }

int rc = xtc_bracket(acq, use, rel, NULL);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xtc_exit_self 3 ,
.Xr xtc_proc 3 ,
.Xr xtc_sync 3 ,
.Xr xtc 7
.Sh HISTORY
Appeared in xtc 0.1.
.Sh CAVEATS
Scopes and masking are per-process
.Pq per-fiber :
they require a running process
.Pq Xr xtc_proc 3 .
Off a process,
.Fn xtc_scope_open
returns
.Dv NULL ,
.Fn xtc_bracket
still honours the acquire/use/release contract directly, and
.Fn xtc_uncancelable
simply runs its body.
